1
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:05,740
- Hey, guys. - Hey.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:06,220
- Hi. - Hey.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,900
We need to talk about something.

4
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:12,280
Yeah. We don't feel like we can host Thanksgiving this year.

5
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,900
- What... - Are you kidding?

6
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:18,960
Well, it's just with work and the stress of adoption we don't feel like we have the energy.

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,500
Plus, we don't think it's fair that every year the burden falls on us.

8
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,780
That doesn't sound like you.

9
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:29,060
That's Monica talking.

10
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:33,880
No, no, we made this decision together.

11
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:35,860
She's putting words in your mouth.

12
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:38,120
Don't you put words in people's mouths.

13
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:39,940
You put turkey in people's mouths.

14
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,560
I can't believe this.

15
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:44,660
This is Emma's first Thanksgiving.

16
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,080
No, it's not.

17
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:47,960
It's not? When was she born?

18
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:51,760
Well, personally,

19
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:53,740
I think it's great you're giving yourself a break.

20
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:54,700
Thank you, Pheebs.

21
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:56,640
Sure. It's just as well.

22
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,200
I mean, last year wasn't very good.

23
00:00:58,280 --> 00:00:59,380
I think she's losing her touch.

24
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,420
What? You are way off, lady.

25
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:05,020
Am l? Really? Am l?

26
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:07,880
Well, why don't you cook Thanksgiving dinner and prove me wrong.

27
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:11,460
Well, think about it.

28
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:13,700
You'd be trying to top what you did last year.

29
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:16,220
You'd be in competition with yourself.

30
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,440
That's my favorite kind.

31
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:22,440
Okay, we are doing this.

32
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:25,300
Don't let yourself get manipulated this way.

33
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:26,720
Stay out of this, Chandler.

34
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:29,040
This is between me and me.

35
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:33,180
We are supposed to make these decisions together.

36
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:36,980
Dr. Phi:一档帮人解决家庭问题的脱口秀

37
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:37,000
Did you not watch the <i>Dr. Phil</i> I taped for you?

38
00:01:39,272 --> 00:01:41,512
《老友记》第十季第八集 感恩节晚餐大家都迟到了

39
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,960
- Hey. - Hi. Happy Thanksgiving.

40
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:36,260
Happy Needless Turkey-Murder Day.

41
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,080
You guys, I ordered some chocolate pies from that bakery on Bleeker.

42
00:02:41,580 --> 00:02:42,520
Could you pick them up for me?

43
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:43,620
You're not making the pies?

44
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,760
I don't make chocolate pies.

45
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:46,760
When I was younger,

46
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,880
I entered this pie-eating contest.

47
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,480
I ate so many that the thought of them makes me sick.

48
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:53,280
Did you at least win the contest?

49
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:56,060
Two minutes, twelve pies and a part of one tin.

50
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,020
Okay, I'll see you guys at 4.

51
00:02:59,160 --> 00:02:59,940
Can't wait.

52
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:02,300
This dinner is gonna be so great.

53
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,320
In your face, last-year me.

54
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:07,720
- Hey, Rach? - Yeah.

55
00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:09,380
What's Emma doing today?

56
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,880
Well, let's see,

57
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:16,360
I know that she has a meeting with her lawyer and then she has to make a very big poop.

58
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:19,340
Why?

59
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:22,080
Well, I want to enter her in a baby pageant.

60
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,200
Oh, my God.

61
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,700
That's the creepiest thing I've ever heard.

62
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:30,360
Okay, but before you say no, my friend Suzanne is entering her kid.

63
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,640
And compared to Emma, she's a real dog.

64
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,940
Phoebe, all babies are beautiful.

65
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:36,680
Oh, okay.

66
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:44,800
No. Phoebe, just the idea of pitting one baby against another l mean, you know, and judging who's cuter just for a trophy...

67
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,780
And a thousand dollars.

68
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:48,580
...is something I'm very interested in.

69
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,500
Oh, please, do not tell Ross.

70
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:54,980
He still believes that what's on the inside is important.

71
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:59,400
Okay. And Emma needs a cowgirl outfit for the competition.

72
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:02,480
Where am I gonna get a cowgirl outfit on Thanksgiving?

73
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:03,380
Well, I was thinking--

74
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:05,780
Take the clothes off Joey's Cabbage Patch Kid!

75
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:17,840
Did someone drop the baton again?

76
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:21,120
Why come all the way from Kansas to do that?

77
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,720
I don't get older, I just get better.

78
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,740
You know what just occurred to me?

79
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:32,400
This could be our last Thanksgiving just the two of us.

80
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,900
I mean, we could be getting a baby soon.

81
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:35,980
You don't know that.

82
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:37,580
Somebody's gonna pick us.

83
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:39,820
But we haven't heard a thing from the adoption agency.

84
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,480
I'm telling you, it's gonna happen.

85
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:46,380
Next year, it's gonna be you, me and little Hemingway Bing.

86
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,460
What? He's my favorite author.

87
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:51,800
Name one of his books.

88
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:58,440
<i>The Firm</i>?

89
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,440
Okay, let's see. Okay, the turkey's in the oven.

90
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:04,600
The stuffing is ready.

91
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:07,120
You know, you always cook this meal all by yourself.

92
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,660
Let me help this year.

93
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:10,320
Oh, Chandler, that's sweet.

94
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:13,100
But you don't have to do everything Dr. Phil tells you to do.

95
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:16,280
I'm serious, let me do something.

96
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:19,277
Just not the turkey. Nothing high-profile.

97
00:05:19,297 --> 00:05:20,380
Okay, let's see.

98
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:22,800
Oh, the cranberry sauce.

99
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:25,200
It's easy to make, and no one really cares about it.

100
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:27,520
Tell me more.

101
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:30,440
I'm gonna go check on something across the hall.

102
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:31,720
You start by washing these.

103
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,000
Not with soap!

104
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:43,420
You obviously haven't tasted my Palmolive potatoes.

105
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:47,980
Hi. Hey, guess what Joey has.

106
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:49,860
Three tickets to today's Rangers game!

107
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:51,560
Dude, I wanted him to guess.

108
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,080
Oh, my God.

109
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,640
Yeah, they're great seats too.

110
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,440
Guess where they are.

111
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:57,120
Center ice.

112
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:01,500
Did I do something to you?

113
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,180
The game's at 1.

114
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,060
So?

115
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,720
Dinner's at 4. We'll never make it back.

116
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:09,180
So we'll leave before it's over.

117
00:06:09,180 --> 00:06:09,940
We'll be back in time.

118
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:10,740
You said that now.

119
00:06:10,750 --> 00:06:12,960
But it could take us a long time to get back home.

120
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:16,560
Plus, Joey could get lost and they could have to page us to go pick him up.

121
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:20,260
Dude, two times that happened!

122
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,720
Look, Monica's been working hard all day.

123
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:26,580
She didn't want to host in the first place.

124
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,360
We shouldn't go.

125
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,540
He's right, man.

126
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:31,440
Yeah, I guess. So we'll see you at 4.

127
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:31,960
Okay.

128
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:34,740
And get ready to taste my very special cranberries.

129
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:37,500
Or should I say "Chan-berries"?

130
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:44,260
That's some gentle comedy, dude.

131
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,960
We're still going to the game, right?

132
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:48,480
Yeah.

133
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:58,580
Hey.

134
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,260
Phoebe, listen, I think we gotta go.

135
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:01,760
This place is freaking me out.

136
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:03,120
I've been watching this guy over there.

137
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:04,500
I don't think he came with a kid.

138
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:07,520
But we can't leave now.

139
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:11,880
There was this one baby, Haley, who was favored to win she got croup, so she had to stay home.

140
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:14,560
This competition just blew wide-open, folks.

141
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,020
Phoebe, it's just too weird.

142
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:20,520
I just saw a 1 -year-old with pantyhose on.

143
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:22,480
Oh, I know. We should've been more prepared.

144
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:28,560
It's okay. Now, the way I see it, our real competition now is Cameron.

145
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:31,000
My God, they just took her sweater off.

146
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,410
Michelin Man:著名轮胎的卡通形象

147
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,400
Look at those arms. Hello, Michelin Man.

148
00:07:33,694 --> 00:07:36,034
Phoebe, come on.

149
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:37,600
You know what, it's already 3:00.

150
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,260
They haven't even gotten to Emma's group yet.

151
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:40,600
We got dinner.

152
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,180
But Emma's got what it takes.

153
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:43,400
She could go all the way!

154
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:47,940
Phoebe, you have to calm down.

155
00:07:48,732 --> 00:07:49,572
Okay.

156
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:56,380
Rachel, the hottest babies in the tri-state area are in this room right now.

157
00:07:57,680 --> 00:08:01,160
I overheard a judge say that not one of them holds a candle to Emma.

158
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,840
- Really? - Yeah.

159
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:04,320
You heard him say that?

160
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:05,440
Yeah.

161
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:10,280
All right. Okay. All right, let's give these babies something to cry about.

162
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:12,900
Good. Let's get down to business.

163
00:08:13,220 --> 00:08:14,080
Emma needs some makeup.

164
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:15,220
What?

165
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,500
She's gonna look washed-out next to the others.

166
00:08:18,070 --> 00:08:20,560
No, Phoebe, I'm not letting you put makeup on my baby.

167
00:08:20,580 --> 00:08:21,240
Why not?

168
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:22,380
Because I already did.

169
00:08:29,696 --> 00:08:33,656
You suck! Get off the ice, you idiot!

170
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:36,860
- What a game. - I know. Yeah.

171
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:39,600
I can't believe Chandler's missing this.

172
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:40,780
I'm sorry he's not here.

173
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:41,600
But I gotta say,

174
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:43,580
I am really enjoying nacho chair.

175
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:48,700
Yeah, I'd probably enjoy it more if you didn't keep batting my hand away.

176
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:53,220
These seats are great.

177
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:54,040
I know, I know.

178
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:59,280
When I was here for "Holidays on lce"  l was sitting so far away,

179
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,180
Michelle Kwan couldn't read my banner.

180
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,870
Michelle Kwan:花样滑冰世界冠军

181
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:04,200
We'd better get going.

182
00:09:04,260 --> 00:09:05,420
If we don't leave now, we're gonna be late.

183
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:07,400
But it's a tie game.

184
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,700
So we're a little late.

185
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:10,060
The girls will be there.

186
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:12,260
Let's just stay for one more goal.

187
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:13,880
- I don't know. - One more fight.

188
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:14,620
- Okay. - Okay.

189
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:20,740
Where is everybody?

190
00:09:20,940 --> 00:09:22,180
They're 45 minutes late.

191
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,680
I can't believe they're not here.

192
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:26,060
I slave and I slave for what?

193
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,160
They've ruined Cranberry Day.

194
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:32,880
How late are we?

195
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:34,060
Forty-five minutes.

196
00:09:34,088 --> 00:09:36,388
- Here. - Okay.

197
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:40,340
Rachel and Phoebe are already there, so they probably started without us.

198
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:42,620
We could just slip in, and no one needs to know where we were.

199
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:47,000
You may want to lose the foam finger.

200
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:49,160
Oh, no, no, no.

201
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,800
You just want to put it on your hand.

202
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:56,920
You're not at Thanksgiving?

203
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:58,940
No, we're late.

204
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:00,340
What are you doing here?

205
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,360
We're late too.

206
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:05,380
We figured we could be late because you'd be on time.

207
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:07,360
Don't point that thing at me, Tribbiani.

208
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:10,100
So nobody's here?

209
00:10:10,260 --> 00:10:11,420
Monica's gonna kill us.

210
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:12,320
Yeah, where were you?

211
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:14,540
Yeah, what's with the trophy?

212
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:17,420
Well, we were at a spelling bee.

213
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:20,520
And I won.

214
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:23,940
You won an adult

215
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:25,980
Thanksgiving Day spelling bee?

216
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:29,200
Yes. Y-E-S. Yes.

217
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:31,160
Let me see this.

218
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:35,420
"Grand Supreme Little Darling, New York Division"?

219
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:36,580
That's me.

220
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:41,540
You entered Emma in a beauty pageant?

221
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:45,680
And it looks like she put makeup on her.

222
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:48,480
Wait a second...

223
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:50,780
Where have I seen that cowgirl outfit before?

224
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:53,760
I can't believe this.

225
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:54,800
She's our daughter.

226
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:58,700
That you would treat her like some kind of show dog is inexcusable.

227
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:00,140
She won a thousand dollars.

228
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:02,460
So this is an annual thing?

229
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:08,260
That's Alicia May Emory's outfit!

230
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:13,880
Guys, there are people in there who are not getting any happier.

231
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:15,180
What are we gonna do?

232
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:16,440
I don't know, you guys figure it out.

233
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,700
I gotta put Emma down for a nap.

234
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:20,040
And, Rach, while you're in there, throw something on Alicia May.

235
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:24,120
All right, what are we gonna say?

236
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,800
We'll say that we were mugged.

237
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:29,740
You can't get mad at someone who's been mugged.

238
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:32,380
Good. But you don't look like you were mugged.

239
00:11:32,696 --> 00:11:34,116
No. Here.

240
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:38,780
Hey!

241
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:42,700
Do you hear something?

242
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:50,920
- They're out there. - Let me see.

243
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,200
I can't believe this.

244
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:56,860
They're an hour late, and they're just standing there talking.

245
00:11:58,820 --> 00:12:00,100
Everything's so distorted.

246
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:03,060
It looks like Joey has a giant hand.

247
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:06,700
That says "Rangers" on it.

248
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:07,740
They went to the game.

249
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:11,800
Oh, they are in for a world of pain.

250
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:15,280
Ross' shirt is torn.

251
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:17,320
They're late and they're sloppy.

252
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:21,180
All right, Emma's napping.

253
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,540
What happened to your shirt?

254
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,260
I got mugged, and they stole my pocket.

255
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:30,340
We're just trying to figure out an excuse.

256
00:12:32,140 --> 00:12:32,840
How about this?

257
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,080
We could say that

258
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,140
Monica told us 5:00, not 4:00.

259
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:37,360
That way we're right on time.

260
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:43,780
Or we could plant PCP in the apartment and call the cops on her.

261
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:49,120
